 "note": "Hashes are over the bytes published at the commit that carries this manifest, and must be re-stamped in any commit that touches a listed file. They pin what was published; they are NOT a reproducibility check, and for four files they cannot be one. growth_curve.json and enumeration_probe.json carry wall-clock timings and are pinned internally by growth_curve.json's `stable_sha256` and enumeration_probe.json's `deterministic_sha256` over their deterministic fields -- both of those reproduce; the whole-file sha here moves per run. crux_quotient_settles.json and probe_answer_key.json have no such internal hash and their `timing_seconds` / `MEASURED.*_seconds` fields move per run too; probe_lp_interface.json says so in its own generator's docstring (B, C and E record their own cost). enumeration_sweep.json is time- and memory-budget driven and reproduces nothing numeric. Re-verified 2026-07-30 after round five: 17 of the then 23 entries matched and 6 did not, every one of the 6 because a later commit (722b6e8e, b43427f0, 9cf779a3, 08820583, 0154c8f1) moved the file without re-stamping the manifest. BASELINE-cycle94.md is tracked in this directory but deliberately unlisted: it is a different concurrent session's cycle log, not an artefact of this run. __pycache__ is excluded: byte-unstable and not an artefact.",
